  "rationale": "The batch repeatedly starts with either a determiner-led description or a name, but the representative continuation after a completed action sentence gives nearly all mass to <END> instead of the observed paragraph break. Add a determiner+noun opening pattern, and a paragraph-break rule for completed object-taking action clauses; its verb set avoids also matching terminal phrases such as “was the end.” Add context-conditioned support for recurring constructions in the revealed documents: capitalized continuation after a paragraph break, conjunction after a one-token name opening, article after a preposition, and the “Long ago,” sequence. These rules generalize over POS or reusable lexical constructions rather than copying whole stories. Counterexamples remain possible: a det+noun phrase need not always end an opening paragraph, a paragraph break need not be followed by And or Long, and not every preposition takes a. The added masses are therefore evidence, not claims that alternatives are impossible; the replay gate must assess the provisional repair."
